5,Afro-Asiatic Languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/afro-asiatic-languages/,"September 5, 2011 - Old South Arabian (extinct), Geez, Tigré, Tigrigna, Dahlik, Gafat, Kistane, Inor, Mesmes, Mesqan, Sebat Bet Gurage, Amharic, Argobba, Harari, Silt’e, Wolane, Zay. ... We have based our classification on the work of Bender (2000). Classification in 6 branches of the Afroasiatic family",Mesme,Afro-Asiatic
6,"From jazz to hip hop, Afro-South Asian music collaborations reflect imagined, more liberatory worlds",https://scroll.in/article/987321/from-jazz-to-hip-hop-afro-south-asian-music-collaborations-reflect-imagined-more-liberatory-worlds,"February 21, 2021 - Davis’ experimental sound on the album was his attempt to make music for “the Black Power generation.” If this was his political impetus and expression of solidarity with disenfranchised Black youth, that he achieved it by putting Afro-diasporic and South Asian instruments and sounds in conversation with one another is revelatory.",Mesme,Afro-Asiatic
7,Afro-Asiatic | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/31/,"Mesme zim, a language of Chad · Musey mse, a language of Chad · Ngete nnn, a language of Chad · Pévé lme, a language of Chad · Zumaya zuy, a language of Cameroon · West 82 · A 45 · A.1 2 · Gwandara gwn, a language of Nigeria · Hausa hau, a language of Nigeria ·",Mesme,Afro-Asiatic
8,Asia After Dark: Afro-Asiatic Mash-up - Smithsonian's National Museum of Asian Art,https://asia-archive.si.edu/asia-after-dark-afro-asiatic-mash-up-2/,"March 25, 2020 - This past Saturday, Freer|Sackler kicked off its wildly popular Asia After Dark event series with a garden party featuring a mash-up performance of Japanese vogue dance, theater, storytelling, and hip-hop music choreographed by visual artist iona rozeal brown and performed by soloist dancer Monstah Black. Guests also created masks using Asian botanical symbols and Ashanti adinkra symbols from West Africa, enjoyed curator-led tours of Hokusai and Perspectives: Ai Weiwei, Afro-disiac cocktails and Sake YUM-YUM shots, a special Chuck Brown tribute, and lots of photo booth fun.",Mesme,Afro-Asiatic
